From: NexRouter Engineering <eng@nexrouter.io>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 01:30:00 +0600
Subject: [PATCH 211/211] mt7615: pipeline-prefetch TX completion tokens in mt7615_mac_tx_free for MIPS 1004Kc

When the MT7615N internal ARM Cortex-R4 MCU (`mt7615_cr4.bin`) returns a batched
`MT_TX_FREE` event containing up to 64 completed TX token IDs, stock
`mt7615_mac_tx_free()` dereferences each `mt76_txwi_cache` and `sk_buff`
sequentially, stalling the 880 MHz MIPS 1004Kc pipeline on cold L1/L2 D-cache
lines for every freed packet.
This patch prefetches the `sk_buff` header in the TX token ring to hide DDR3
latency during high-speed 64-MPDU bursts.

--- a/mt7615/mac.c
+++ b/mt7615/mac.c
@@ -1320,6 +1320,8 @@ static void mt7615_mac_tx_free(struct mt7615_dev *dev, void *data, int len)
 		txwi = mt76_token_release(mdev, wlan_idx, &wake);
 		if (!txwi)
 			continue;
+		if (txwi->skb)
+			prefetch(txwi->skb);
 
 		mt76_connac2_txwi_free(mdev, txwi, sta, &free_list);
 	}
